// src/v4/lens/testgen.dag
//
// Scope: testgen lens — reads substrate declarations and produces TestClaim
//        instances structurally. The producer side of "tests are data, not
//        code" (THESIS facet 3). Output is consumed by lens/coverage.dag
//        which verifies the produced set covers the expected substrate
//        cross-product.
// Anchor: TESTING.md §"Test layers (target ratios)" + THESIS.md §348-368
//         "Tests are structural data" + §168-182 correctness tiers +
//         memory: feedback_groundedness_gates_lenses (testgen applies
//         to every program by construction)
//
// Owns:
//   - Generator<C> generic carrier (parameterized over substrate concept)
//   - Per-substrate-kind testgen rules:
//     - type_construction(Atom | Conj | Disj | ...) -> Set<Constructible TestClaim>
//     - algebra_law(Algebra × Inhabitant × Law) -> Set<Equals TestClaim>
//     - diagnostic_exhaustiveness(NamedReason variant) -> Set<DiagnosticEmitted TestClaim>
//     - lens_applicability(Lens × Program) -> Set<LensProducesResult TestClaim>
//     - bidirectional_roundtrip(Language × GrammarProduction) -> Set<BitEqual TestClaim>
//   - TestClassification = (Tier, Layer) for every produced claim
//     - Tier: Tier1 | Tier2 | Tier3 (THESIS correctness tier)
//     - Layer: Unit | Integration | Boundary (TESTING.md test layer)
//   - lens read: () -> Set<TestClaim>  (the produced corpus)
//
// Tier × Layer cross-cut discipline (per TESTING.md ratio targets):
//   - Unit tests target ~75%: type-construction, exhaustiveness, lens-applicability
//   - Integration tests target ~15%: cross-stage invariants, fixed-point convergence
//   - Boundary tests target ~10%: language roundtrips (rustc/python/go/cpp/ts), L4 runtime equivalence
//   - testgen output respecting these ratios is structurally enforceable via coverage lens
//
// Bootstrap path:
//   - test/claim/manual/ holds hand-authored TestClaims authored after T-1 lands
//   - testgen (T-19) produces the same corpus programmatically
//   - Assertion: testgen-produced set ⊇ manual set; manual claims are
//     anti-regression anchors against testgen drift
//
// Consumes:
//   - std/node.dag (substrate to walk)
//   - std/algebra.dag (algebra inhabitance for L7-class testgen)
//   - std/verification.dag (TestClaim output schema)
//   - std/diagnostic.dag (Diagnostic.NamedReason for exhaustiveness testgen)
//   - lens/*.dag (each lens's declared read shape, for applicability testgen)
//   - extdeps/languages/*.dag (bidirectional roundtrip testgen)
//
// Status: scaffold — fill per TASKS.md T-19
// Brief: see BRIEF_TEMPLATE.md. T-19 is Phase 1.5 — right after std/*
// substrate (T-1/T-2/T-3) lands, BEFORE compiler stages (T-6+) start.
// This buys test evidence early — every Phase 2+ task gets a testgen-
// derived corpus instead of hand-authoring.

module v4.lens.testgen

